# The White Oak — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. Never commit `.env.local`.
# See `.gitignore` — `.env*` is excluded.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL (drives absolute URLs for OG image, canonical link, etc.)
#
# Priority order in app/layout.tsx:
#   1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL  — set this once you cut DNS to the custom domain
#   2. VERCEL_URL            — auto-injected by Vercel per deploy; current fallback
#   3. http://localhost:3000 — dev fallback
#
# In Vercel: set under Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://thewhiteoakhouston.com

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Propertybase / Salesforce
#
# The lead capture endpoint at /api/subscribe will POST a pba__Request__c
# Inquiry to the Salesforce REST API. Wiring isn't done yet — these vars
# document what the API route will need once auth is decided.
#
# Auth approach is TBD: server-to-server Client Credentials Flow is the
# likely pick (no per-user OAuth required). Until then, the route logs the
# PB-shaped payload server-side instead of POSTing.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the Salesforce org (e.g. https://nan-properties.my.salesforce.com).
# Used to construct API URLs like {INSTANCE_URL}/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/pba__Request__c
# PROPERTYBASE_INSTANCE_URL=

# OAuth access token for the integration user / Connected App. If we land on
# Client Credentials Flow, this is short-lived (~2h) and the route refreshes
# it as needed; we'd add PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_ID and PROPERTYBASE_CLIENT_SECRET
# below and remove this static token.
# PROPERTYBASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
